VeridianOS: port libksysguard off deprecated Qt/KF6 API (QVariant::Type, KLocalizedContext, QMap iterator +)

GCC reported -Wdeprecated-declarations for:

- QVariant::Type ("Use QMetaType::Type instead") in SensorInfo.h:32/76,
  SensorProperty.h:84, SensorProperty.cpp:164, Sensor.h:159, Sensor.cpp:161,
  and QVariant::QVariant(Type) in Sensor.cpp:169. Ported to QMetaType::Type:
  SensorInfo::variantType (both the public systemstats/SensorInfo.h and the
  installed sensors/SensorInfo_p.h copy, so the two definitions of
  KSysGuard::SensorInfo stay identical), SensorProperty::setVariantType(),
  Sensor::type() and its Q_PROPERTY, and QVariant{QMetaType(type)} for the
  default value. QVariant::Type's enumerators are defined as the QMetaType
  values, so every stored value is the same number.
  Two places had to keep the old representation explicitly:
  * D-Bus: QVariant::Type has a 0xffffffff enumerator, so its underlying type
    is unsigned and "argument << s.variantType" marshalled a uint ("u", as
    the org.kde.ksystemstats1 XML declares: (sssuuddi)). QMetaType::Type is
    int-sized and would marshal as "i" and break the wire format, so the
    value is now streamed as static_cast<uint>(...). The reader already read
    a uint32_t.
  * SensorDataModel TypeRole: "return info.variantType;" produced a QVariant
    holding that uint; QVariant(QMetaType::Type) is a deleted constructor, so
    it now returns static_cast<uint>(info.variantType), the same QVariant.
  This changes the C++ API/ABI of libksysguard (setVariantType and
  Sensor::type take/return QMetaType::Type). The only in-tree caller,
  ksystemstats, passes QVariant::Double etc. to setVariantType and needs the
  companion ksystemstats patch (QVariant::X -> QMetaType::X); everything is
  rebuilt from source in order, so the soname is not bumped.
- QVariant::type() in SensorFaceController.cpp:940: use typeId() and
  QMetaType::QStringList (same comparison).
- KLocalizedContext (deprecated since KF 6.8) in SensorFaceController_p.h:104
  and SensorFaceController.cpp:396: use KLocalizedQmlContext from
  KF6::I18nQml (same parent, same setTranslationDomain() and i18n*()
  context-object API used by the face QML); SensorFaces now links
  KF6::I18nQml (KF6 >= 6.26 is already required).
  KLocalizedQmlContext adds what KLocalizedContext lacked: it installs a
  process-wide event filter that retranslates on a language change, and
  each i18n*() call tries to mark the calling binding as a translation
  binding. This context object has no QML engine of its own, so that
  attempt only logs a kf.i18n.qml debug message; translations are
  unchanged.
- QMap iterator + int in SensorUnitModel.cpp:104 ("QMap iterators are not
  random access"): use std::next() (same element).

Not handled here: "'TRANSLATION_DOMAIN' redefined" (0001); the
Formatter.cpp 'inputOrder' warning is fixed in 0003 (real bug).

